---
// The Browse trigger. Placed OUTSIDE the reader grid on purpose: a sibling of `.reader-layout`,
// never its third grid child, or it becomes a phantom grid item at desktop width. The labelled
// "Browse" pill is the DESKTOP trigger (CSS-shown only at >=1024px); at every width the reader
// menu's Contents row (islands/reader/menu) opens the same drawer by event. It wears the library
// glyph (books on a shelf), as does the problem page's pill: it says what the drawer is for — the
// whole shelf, not the one book open. A stroked `currentColor` glyph rather than an emoji, so it
// matches every other control and follows the theme. Its accessible name is the word the drawer
// heading shows. The pill opens the drawer, which clones `.reader-sidebar .reader-sidebar__inner`
// at click time (islands/reader.ts) and sits OVER the page — the desktop sidebar stays as it is.
// Shared by the server-rendered lesson and the private shell.
---

<div class="reader-nav">
  <button class="reader-contents-pill" aria-label="Browse — every lesson in this book" aria-expanded="false" type="button">
    <svg
      class="reader-contents-pill__ic"
      viewBox="0 0 24 24"
      fill="none"
      stroke="currentColor"
      stroke-width="2"
      stroke-linecap="round"
      stroke-linejoin="round"
      aria-hidden="true"
    >
      <path d="m16 6 4 14 M12 6v14 M8 8v12 M4 4v16" />
    </svg>
    <span>Browse</span>
  </button>
</div>
